==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mecha-Bun Mk II''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Mecha-Bun''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP after completing [[An Ancient Curse]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Mecha-Bun is overall mediocre due to its low stats. For starter, it has a decent amount of 54.4K HP in general; which is enough to take a few hits from {{4c}} SoL enemies, but in later game, that amount of health is too lackluster to boot. Next is its offense, being only 6.8K damage and 6.5K DPS which are rather low for Melee rusher standards, as these units demand high burst damage to make up for their fragile and disposable nature.

Assuming that you don't have anything better to use, Mecha-Bun is okay at rushing on {{4c}} and can deliver somewhat okayish amount of DPS. However, this is assuming that you don't have anything better to use, as there are even more reliable sources of DPS like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] as their spammability and great offense make Mecha-Bun useless. It still has an use as a secondary rusher that can tank, if you don't have [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] yet, though even a high leveled [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]] is even better due to his decent cost efficiency to provide less defense and offense yet can be spammed.

==='''True Form'''===
Ultimate Mecha-Bun gains the Strong Against ability vs. Relics, higher health and attack power, and a slightly longer attack rate. Unfortunately, aside from usage against Relics, none of this increases its base stats enough to matter, so you should not unlock it unless you are especially struggling against Relics—specifically [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]], [[Lowkey]], or potentially [[Oldhorn]], as it can deal a fair bit of damage to them before requiring replacement, eased by its faster cooldown. Other [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic units]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] make a better use of Elder Catfruit, meaning that unlocking Ultimate Mecha-Bun should not be a priority until [[Primitive Souls]] is reached and has to be done in multiple difficulties; provided if you do not have units suitable for this stage.

