==Trivia==
*Mecha-Bun is the only [[Stories of Legend]] drop unit whose Normal Form doesn't have a preview shown when entering [[Legend Stages]]. It is also one of the only three [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] whose True Form has a preview, other than [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]].
**Even though Mecha-Bun is supposed to come as a surprise, the player can spoil its name for themselves through the ''Buns of Steel'' [[Meow Medals|Meow Medal]]'s description, which becomes visible after unlocking [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]].
*It and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]] are the only Stories of Legend drop units to have a 100% drop rate.
*Its Normal Form's Japanese description is one of the few to directly mention a sub-chapter by name. The others are the [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus Enemies]]' descriptions, which also refer to the [[Laboratory of Relics]], and [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]]'s description, which mentions [[Humanity Catified]].
*Due to the presence of extra frames in both the Normal and True Forms' attack animations, Mecha Bun's Evolved Form is the only one with the same exact attack frequency as [[Teacher Bun Bun]].
*[[Bun Bun Monger Prototype (PC Special Cat)|Bun Bun Monger Prototype]] may have foreshadowed or simply been early designs of Mecha-Bun and its forms, given that they were released approximately 8 months before [[Version 7.0 Update|Version 7.0]], in [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou]].
**The "ancient prototype schematics" mentioned in both the English and Japanese descriptions may even be a reference to Bun Bun Monger Prototype.

